+# Block40 prospective conditional scaling boundary
+
+2026-09-07. Root exposed the exponential-clustering/polynomial-renormalization candidate before this contract. No completed root proof has been read and no new finite calculation has been run.
+
+Target: a precise conditional vanishing theorem for connected ground correlations at positive fixed physical separation when lattice spacing ell tends to zero, u=av remains in one fixed sufficiently small window with uniform imported clustering constants, observable supports contain a fixed bounded number of cells in bounded lattice radius, and observable norms grow at most a fixed polynomial in ell^-1. Extend only to smearing sums whose total coefficient l1 norm grows polynomially and whose two physical support regions remain positively separated.
+
+Explicit falsifiers/scope: polynomial bounds are essential; exponential norm factors can cancel clustering. Fixed physical diameter observables need not have bounded lattice supports. Coincident/contact correlations and distributions on the diagonal are not controlled. Moving toward a regime where the imported clustering constants are nonuniform is excluded. The result is not a no-go for all continuum limits.
+
+Independent dynamics check: use gap34 lower2/a and LR35 upper32e v in link distance, with independent supplied spatial spacing ell and clock scale tau=b_ell t. Derive only bounds; never equate a with ell or LR velocity with measured/actual speed. Check whether a uniformly bounded actual rescaled gap forces the LR velocity upper to vanish, and whether a fixed nonzero allowed velocity requires divergent gap lower. This is a conditional tradeoff, not a dispersion theorem.
+
+Primary imports: Yarotsky0412040 Theorem1(3)/Section2 and the reviewed fixed-model34/35 bounds. No new generic exponential-clustering novelty is claimed. Preserve any missing uniformity/domain assumption. No repository writes.
